      "writtenOn": "2024-06-25T18:28:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What about methods declared by Object, such as toString or hashCode? Or from Parcelable, such as writeToParcel? I guess we call getCallbackIdsCallingThisMethod, loop through the array, and return early when it finds no match? Would something like:\n\n    // Ignore methods declared by NetworkCallback itself, Parcelable, etc.\n    if (classMethod.getDeclaringClass().isAssignableFrom(NetworkCallback.class)) {\n\nbe better due to skipping the iteration?\n\nAnd actually - could/should this code use clazz.getDeclaredMethods to list only the methods defined by this class? Or does that not work, because the methods are not defined by this class, but defined by NetworkCallback and overridden by this class?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 4775,
        "startChar": 51,
        "endLine": 4775,
        "endChar": 72
      },
      "revId": "cc28c8c24556b670cd8f6c46f88a45f27955bed0",
